   "answer": "## Final answer: nine-run qualification of the LASV IgG ELISA\n\n**LLOQ = 0.121 IU/mL (STD\\*-7). ULOQ = 7.744 IU/mL (STD\\*-1).** This follows your request text, which requires a CV below 25% for both OD and concentration. The LLOQ depends on that reading, so see the question below.\n\n### Corrections from the review\n- **R² and recovery values:** I did not run compare_options, so no number comes from a comparison run. The R² values 0.9997 (plates 1 and 5) are from the chosen 4PL fit. The 75% is the lower bound of your recovery window, not a result.\n- **Blank value 0.146:** confirmed by the script output. Run 1 blank R1-Blank-2 reads 0.146. The other run 1 blanks read 0.023, 0.015 and 0.014.\n- **LLOQ reading:** your request says CV below 25% \"for both the OD and the concentration\". Under that reading STD\\*-8 fails on OD CV (26.62%), so the LLOQ is 0.121 IU/mL. If only the concentration CV counts, STD\\*-8 (0.060 IU/mL) passes with a concentration CV of 15.55% and recovery of 92.99%, and the LLOQ becomes 0.060 IU/mL. I kept the rule as you wrote it. Please confirm which reading you want.\n\n### Settings and steps\n- **Model:** 4PL (the tool's fit). I did not see a recorded answer for the curve model, so please confirm.\n- **Weighting:** none. **Blank correction:** none. **Replicates:** signals averaged per run before the fit.\n- **LOD:** blank mean plus 3 SD. **Accepted bias:** 25%. **CV limit:** 25%.\n- **Excluded wells:** R7-LPC-2 and R9-LPC-1, both masked in the reader software. The refit matched the first run, so the record already held these exclusions.\n- **Dilution factor:** 1 for all wells, because the file has no dilution column. The nominal values are taken as the concentrations of the dilutions.\n- **drc version:** the adapter lists drc 4.6.1. The tool output I read does not print the version string.\n- **Steps:** I fitted each run (9 runs, 10 standards with 2 replicate wells each), checked the fits, summarised each dilution and control across the runs with a script (saved as qualification_summary.csv), and applied the LLOQ/ULOQ rule.\n\n### Fit quality per run (tool output)\n- R-squared: 0.9997, 0.9999, 0.9999, 0.9999, 0.9997, 0.9999, 0.9993, 1, 0.9999 (runs 1 to 9).\n\n### Dilutions and controls, mean over the 9 runs\nMean OD and mean concentration are the means of the per-run values. CV is the sample SD over runs divided by the mean. Recovery is the mean concentration over nominal.\n\n| Sample | Nominal (IU/mL) | Mean OD (CV %) | Mean conc (IU/mL) (CV %) | Recovery % | Passes rule (both OD and conc CV) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| STD\\*-1 | 7.744 | 2.8867 (11.93) | 7.5869 (11.07) | 97.97 | yes |\n| STD\\*-2 | 3.872 | 2.2355 (14.60) | 3.7072 (8.73) | 95.74 | yes |\n| STD\\*-3 | 1.936 | 1.5657 (15.40) | 1.8719 (11.39) | 96.69 | yes |\n| STD\\*-4 | 0.968 | 0.9767 (18.77) | 0.9171 (10.93) | 94.74 | yes |\n| STD\\*-5 | 0.484 | 0.5754 (17.96) | 0.4637 (9.21) | 95.81 | yes |\n| STD\\*-6 | 0.242 | 0.3264 (19.94) | 0.2334 (8.79) | 96.45 | yes |\n| STD\\*-7 | 0.121 | 0.1871 (21.92) | 0.1205 (15.71) | 99.55 | yes |\n| STD\\*-8 | 0.060 | 0.1030 (26.62) | 0.0558 (15.55) | 92.99 | no (OD CV) |\n| STD\\*-9 | 0.030 | 0.0626 (35.00) | 0.0266 (25.89) | 88.71 | no (OD and conc CV) |\n| STD\\*-10 | 0.015 | 0.0412 (48.35) | 0.0139 (42.04), n = 8 | 92.56 | no (OD and conc CV) |\n| HPC (control) | 1.858 | 1.6177 (21.49) | 1.9932 (22.45) | 107.28 | not a dilution |\n| LPC (control) | 0.465 | 0.5723 (25.33) | 0.4569 (20.03) | 98.25 | not a dilution |\n\n- STD\\*-10 has 8 runs with a concentration. In run 1 its OD (0.0355) lies below the lower asymptote, so the curve gives no concentration there.\n- LPC's OD CV (25.33%) is just above 25%. It is a control, so it does not enter the LLOQ or ULOQ rule.\n\n### Points to check\n- **Blank in run 1:** R1-Blank-2 (0.146) is well above the other run 1 blanks (0.014 to 0.023). It inflates the run 1 blank SD and so the run 1 LOD. I did not exclude it, because you named only two wells.\n- **LOD by run (IU/mL, tool output):** run 1 0.1619; runs 2, 3 and 4 undefined (the 3-SD blank signal lies below the fitted lower asymptote); run 5 0.00092; run 6 0.00066; run 7 0.0186; run 8 0.0054; run 9 0.0165. The spread is wide, so I would not quote one LOD until the blank question is settled.\n- **Per-run standard LLOQ (tool, 25% bias rule):** 0.29 IU/mL in run 1, 0.036 in runs 7 and 9, and 0.018 in the other runs. This is a separate rule from the dilution rule. The standard ULOQ is 9.292 IU/mL in every run.\n- **Dilution factor:** if the dilutions were made on top of the nominal values, the concentrations change by that factor.\n\n### What is uncertain\n- The LLOQ depends on how the CV rule is read (both OD and concentration, or concentration alone). It gives 0.121 IU/mL or 0.060 IU/mL.\n- The LOD depends on the blank question above.\n\n### What waits for the scientist\n- Confirm the LLOQ rule: both OD and concentration CV (LLOQ 0.121 IU/mL), or concentration CV only (LLOQ 0.060 IU/mL).\n- Confirm 4PL as the curve model.\n- Decide whether R1-Blank-2 is an outlier.\n- Say whether the ULOQ should be reported as 7.744 IU/mL or as \"at least\" that value.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n5 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/yun2026-lasv-elisa/run1/home/sessions/20261008-230845-6caa/work and wrote 1 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/yun2026-lasv-elisa/run1/home/sessions/20261008-230845-6caa/work.\n- n6 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/yun2026-lasv-elisa/run1/home/sessions/20261008-230845-6caa/work and wrote 0 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/yun2026-lasv-elisa/run1/home/sessions/20261008-230845-6caa/work.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: